// @ens-test
// @exit 2
// @stdout-contains PASS first test passes
// @stdout-contains panic: boom
// @stdout-contains crash_test.ens
// @stderr-contains stopped while running 'second test panics'
// @stderr-contains --filter 'second test panics'
// A panic in the second test ends the whole run. The first result is already out,
// because the command passes each line on as the test producing it finishes; the
// panic arrives on the same stream, in the place it happened, because a child's two
// streams reach the command as one. The command counted the results as they went
// past, so what it adds on its own error stream names the test that was running.
